# Agent workflow

Read @.ai/rules/agent-workflow.md and follow it before implementing, creating a branch, opening or updating a pull request, or changing plan status. That file is the canonical workflow.

- A human approves the specific plan step and its acceptance criteria before implementation.
- One approved plan step per branch and pull request. Branch from the latest `main` as `step/<plan-step-id>-<slug>`.
- If the step is ambiguous, crosses module boundaries, or depends on unfinished work, stop and ask.
- "Evaluate", "assess", "check alignment", and "review" mean analysis only. Report findings, then wait.
- After opening the pull request, stop. Do not merge, start the next step, or add unrelated changes.
- Record canonical status only in the plan that owns that work item, in the pull request that changes it.
- In a test-first step, the implementer never changes the tests or stub signatures from the reviewed `<plan-step-id>: tests first` commit; if one looks wrong, stop and report it.
- Run the relevant checks in @.ai/scripts/verify.md. Never use `--no-verify`.
